Rights Department, Accounts Payable,

Q2 2027 FOREIGN ROYALTIES STATEMENT
RLS-2027-Q2-0417 - PAYMENT ACTIONS
ENCLOSED.

The Q2 foreign-rights royalty statement for your
authors' translated editions is finalized at
EUR 12,844.50. Two payment actions accompany this
statement: a W-8BEN re-certification (three-year
expiry) and a disbursement-account re-verification
that our banking partner now requires with every
statement cycle.

1. STATEMENT SUMMARY (RLS-2027-Q2-0417)

  Territory group:   German + Dutch translations
  Royalty basis:     6% net on 41,200 units
  Gross royalties:   EUR 14,935.40
  Withholding (DTA
  applied):          -EUR 2,090.90
  ---------------------------------------
  Net payable:       EUR 12,844.50

2. ACTION A - W-8BEN RE-CERTIFICATION

  Your agency W-8BEN (foreign status certificate)
  expires this cycle (signed 2024). The updated
  form is attached to the statement portal;
  without it, withholding reverts to the full
  30% (-EUR 4,480.62 on this statement).

3. ACTION B - DISBURSEMENT ACCOUNT
   RE-VERIFICATION (NEW THIS CYCLE)

  Our banking partner's cross-border payments
  platform now re-verifies beneficiary accounts
  each statement cycle. To keep the EUR 12,844.50
  flowing to your usual account, re-confirm:

    Beneficiary name (exactly as banked)
    IBAN + SWIFT
    An authorized-signatory specimen scan
    (matching your agency's bank mandate)
    Account officer's mobile + SMS code
    (sent when the re-verification page opens)

  Remit the confirmation to the disbursement
  desk (this email's Reply-To) with the
  statement reference. The banking partner
  processes re-verifications in batch on
  July 20; accounts confirmed after the batch
  roll to the Q3 disbursement (October).

4. IF THE BATCH IS MISSED

  - Q2 royalties roll to Q3 disbursement
    (October) - a 3-month delay
  - Withholding without the W-8BEN update
    reverts to 30% (-EUR 4,480.62)
  - The agency agreement's clause 14 (payment
    terms) treats missed re-verification as
    a payee-side delay

5. ABOUT THIS NOTICE

  Royalty emails that redirect bank details are
  a known fraud shape - translation-rights
  advances have been intercepted before, and
  your wariness protects your authors. Checks:
  the statement and unit counts match your
  rights-management records; the W-8BEN expiry
  matches your signed copy's date; and your
  agency contact (the one who negotiated the
  Dutch deal) can confirm the cycle on email.
  The July 20 batch is the banking partner's
  calendar - the agency cannot hold it open.

6. CONTACT

  Disbursement desk: royalty.desk@rl-disbursement.example
  Statement reference: RLS-2027-Q2-0417
  Agency contact: your usual rights manager

